HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:3:description: Guide to SGLang CI workflow orchestration — stage ordering, fast-fail, gating, partitioning, execution modes, and debugging CI failures. Use when modifying CI workflows, adding stages, debugging CI pipeline issues, or understanding how tests are dispatched and gated across stages.
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:135:- **Layer 3**: `check-pr-test-health` auto-detects `schedule` event and skips; filters out cascade failures to show only root cause jobs
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:146:| **continue-on-error** | No (stop at first failure within suite) | Yes (run all tests) | No |
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:150:| **Concurrency** | `cancel-in-progress: true` per branch | Queue (no cancel) | Isolated per stage+SHA |
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:161:3. If any matched job has `conclusion === 'failure'` → fail immediately (fast-fail)
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:188:2. Filters for **root cause failures only** — jobs with `conclusion === 'failure'` whose failing step is NOT `check-pr-test-health` (excludes cascade failures)
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:189:3. If root cause failures found → calls `core.setFailed()` with the list of root cause job names
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:192:**Cascade filtering**: When job A fast-fails due to health check, it also has `conclusion: failure`. Without filtering, job B would list both the original failure AND job A's fast-fail. The filter checks each failed job's `steps` array — if the failing step name contains `check-pr-test-health` or `Check PR test health`, it's excluded from the root cause list.
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:211:**Visual effect**: Job shows **red X** (failure) with error annotation showing root cause job names. Subsequent steps are naturally skipped (default `if: success()` is false after a failed step). No per-step `if` guards needed.
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:213:**No stage filtering**: Checks ALL jobs in the run, not just the current stage. Any failure anywhere triggers fast-fail.
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:222:## Within-Suite Failure Handling
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:230:| `--continue-on-error` | Off | On | Off: stop at first failure. On: run all files, report all failures at end |
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:231:| `--enable-retry` | On | On | Retry retriable failures (accuracy/perf assertions) |
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:244:**Default**: Unknown `AssertionError` → retriable. Other unknown failures → not retriable.
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:345:`cancel-in-progress: true` for `pull_request` events (new push cancels old run), `false` for `workflow_call`.
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:367:## How To: Debug CI Failures
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:373:| `pr-test-finish` fails but all jobs green | A job was `cancelled` (counts as failure in finish) | Check concurrency cancellation |
HEAD:.claude/skills/ci-workflow-guide/SKILL.md:375:| Flaky test retried and passed | Retriable failure (accuracy/perf) | Check `[CI Retry]` markers in job logs |
