codex
ROLE: systems_reviewer  VOTE: red
EXISTING_IMPLEMENTATIONS: [
  {system: "Mavi et al. 2025, Self-Evaluating LLMs for Multi-Step Tasks", url: "https://openreview.net/pdf?id=AWL1j8u2PH", overlap: "Direct: online/stepwise confidence scoring for multi-step failure detection; packet reports AUC-ROC about 0.9, above CLAIM-0037 monitor AUC 0.743."},
  {system: "Vasudev et al. 2026, Accurate Failure Prediction in Agents...", url: "https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.03338", overlap: "Direct/near-direct: LLM critic predicts agent failure; packet reports AUROC 0.94, dominating the monitor regime."},
  {system: "AgentBoard", url: "https://proceedings.neurips.cc/paper_files/paper/2024/hash/877b40688e330a0e2a3fc24084208dfa-Abstract-Datasets_and_Benchmarks_Tra", overlap: "Partial: progress-rate/subgoal-progress evaluation for multi-turn agents; post-hoc/annotation-dependent, not full online lead-time monitor."},
  {system: "Let's Verify Step by Step / PRMs", url: "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.20050", overlap: "Partial: online-compatible step-level process scoring, though not agent lead-time failure detection."},
  {system: "vLLM / SGLang / LMCache / FlashInfer / TensorRT-LLM", url: "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm ; https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang ; https://github.com/LMCache/LMCache ; https://github.com/flashinfer-ai/flashinfer ; https://github.com/NVIDIA/TensorRT-LLM", overlap: "OSS repo search found serving/runtime/kernel/cache/CI monitoring uses, not a shipped online agent trajectory failure-warning mechanism."}
]
CONTRIBUTION_TYPE: integration-only
SCALE_REALISM: Does not hold on the provided evidence. The artifact is L0 CPU simulation, not real tau-bench/AppWorld/SWE-agent rollouts. Lead-time coverage is 42.4% >=1 step early, below the pre-registered >0.5 bar. At realistic strong stepwise-evaluator calibration from cited prior work, about 0.9 AUROC, the packet's own sweep says the monitor loses.
RATIONALE: prompt_version=v001. RED because the load-bearing systems claim is already occupied by online/stepwise failure detection prior art, and the claimed external monitor only beats naive verbalized confidence after confidence AUROC drops below about 0.72. It does not beat modeled self-confidence at sigma_conf=0.35, d=-0.006 CI [-0.011,-0.001], and published stepwise/critic baselines cited in the packet report about 0.9/0.94 AUROC. The robust +0.095 over static difficulty is insufficient as a systems insight because PRM/progress-rate systems already cover step/progress scoring, and the surviving lead-time framing failed its own L0 threshold.
